# review.conf — per-project settings for the review hooks.
#
# Copy this file to `review.conf` in the same directory and edit. It is plain
# shell, sourced by lib/review-core.sh, so keep it to the assignments below.
# Every value uses `${VAR:-default}` so an environment override on the command
# line (`REVIEW_MODEL=... git commit`) still wins.

# Model the reviewer runs with. The `claude` CLI is used when it is on PATH;
# otherwise ANTHROPIC_API_KEY plus curl and python3 talk to the API directly.
REVIEW_MODEL="${REVIEW_MODEL:-claude-sonnet-5}"

# Directories git-grep searches for callers and dangling references when it
# builds the prompt. "." is the whole tree. Narrow it on a repo with large
# docs or fixtures so the reviewer is not shown matches from prose.
#   REVIEW_SOURCE_DIRS="src lib"
REVIEW_SOURCE_DIRS="${REVIEW_SOURCE_DIRS:-.}"

# Extra shell globs, space-separated, that are never worth a review pass. The
# built-in list already skips lockfiles, binary assets, vendored trees and
# generated code.
#   REVIEW_EXTRA_IGNORE="docs/* *.snap fixtures/*"
REVIEW_EXTRA_IGNORE="${REVIEW_EXTRA_IGNORE:-}"

# A static check to run over the staged reviewable files before the model
# sees them. Invoked from the repo root as `$REVIEW_LINT_CMD <file>...`; a
# non-zero exit blocks the commit without a model call. Leave empty to skip.
# Examples:
#   REVIEW_LINT_CMD="selene --allow-warnings --quiet"          # Luau
#   REVIEW_LINT_CMD="npx eslint --max-warnings=-1"             # JS/TS
#   REVIEW_LINT_CMD="ruff check"                               # Python
#   REVIEW_LINT_CMD="shellcheck -S error"                      # shell
REVIEW_LINT_CMD="${REVIEW_LINT_CMD:-}"

# Timeouts, in seconds. The base covers the first REVIEW_TIMEOUT_STEP_BYTES
# of prompt; every further step adds REVIEW_TIMEOUT_STEP_SECS, capped at
# REVIEW_TIMEOUT_MAX. A timeout fails open (the commit goes through, is
# ledgered, and is re-reviewed at push), so err on the generous side.
REVIEW_TIMEOUT="${REVIEW_TIMEOUT:-180}"
REVIEW_TIMEOUT_MAX="${REVIEW_TIMEOUT_MAX:-600}"

# Changed lines in one file before its full current text is attached to the
# prompt as context, and the byte budgets for the diff and those attachments.
REVIEW_CONTEXT_THRESHOLD="${REVIEW_CONTEXT_THRESHOLD:-30}"
REVIEW_MAX_DIFF_BYTES="${REVIEW_MAX_DIFF_BYTES:-200000}"
REVIEW_MAX_CONTEXT_BYTES="${REVIEW_MAX_CONTEXT_BYTES:-60000}"
